# mtkcore-154-rcp: IEEE 802.15.4 variant in OpenThread Radio Co-Processor mode.
#
#   idf.py -D SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.154;sdkconfig.154-rcp" build
#
# Layered on sdkconfig.154, which already compiles the Bluetooth controller
# and the captive portal out to fund the memory.
#
# The ESP32-C6 is the radio co-processor; the Thread stack runs on the host
# over Spinel. Core builds no Thread application stack.
#
# The raw 802.15.4 opcodes (0x0007/0x0001..0x0007) are UNAVAILABLE in this
# image: OpenThread's port layer owns the 802.15.4 driver's completion
# callbacks, and the driver has exactly one owner, so raw radio access and
# RCP cannot coexist in one binary. A host selects the image it needs and
# discovers what it got through GET_CAPABILITIES, never by variant name.
CONFIG_OPENTHREAD_ENABLED=y
CONFIG_OPENTHREAD_RADIO=y
